# CHEMSMART PySCF driver
"""PySCF driver generated by CHEMSMART.

DO NOT EDIT: this file is regenerated on every run, so edits are lost.
Rerun it directly with `python <this file>` to reproduce the calculation.

Imports pyscf, numpy, h5py and the standard library only -- never chemsmart.
That keeps CHEMSMART's numpy pin and dependency tree out of the compute
process, so a job can run in its own environment.

CHEMSMART also imports this module for the results-file contract
(``write_pyscf_h5`` and the constants below), so the fake runner and the
reader share one definition with the generated script. Importing it runs no
chemistry: pyscf is imported only inside the functions that need it, and the
configuration is parsed only when run as a script.
"""

